] [17592186074616 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "18311dd6-9a0a-534e-9a8d-3794869d485b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074616 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074617 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074617 #edb/ref 1061 17330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074617 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b3df2fe0-94ac-5bcc-a3b1-52b4d1b4236b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074617 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074618 #edb/ref 1061 17331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074618 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "347b63ef-9c0b-5688-8e27-d7df776461a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074618 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074629 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074629 #edb/ref 1061 18413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074629 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7987d98c-69c0-57a6-b100-cd3d9e53820b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074629 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186075005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075005 #edb/ref 1064 "Unit rates can be used to solve many real-world problems in which we are given two quantities and wish to find what happens to one quantity when we vary the other.\n\nFor example, we might know the total cost of a specific number of items and be asked to find the cost for a different number of the same item.\n\nTo solve a problem using unit rates, the first step is to compute the unit rate by dividing the two given quantities. Then, we can use the unit rate to calculate the desired quantity.\n\nLet's see some examples!" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075005 #edb/ref 1065 3313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075005 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "fc623ecb-782c-5182-90e7-e8b6720b2780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075005 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
